course: dictionary
lesson: 1566
title: Context clues: chaplain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chaplain is a religious leader who works somewhere other than a church. Chaplains work in schools, hospitals, prisons, the army, universities and sports teams. The word tells you the job: they care for people in those places.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence. «A hospital chaplain is a religious leader who visits patients and families.» Hospital tells you where, visits tells you what they do, and patients and families tell you who they help. You can work out a lot before you check the dictionary.
explain: Look at «Many hospitals have chaplains from different faiths who comfort patients and families.» Faiths means religions, so chaplains can belong to different religions. Comfort means helping people feel better when they are worried or upset.
explain: Now test your guess. Swap in "a helper who looks after people" and read the sentence again. It still makes sense, so your guess is close. The dictionary gives the exact meaning: a religious leader who works outside a church.
fact: A chaplain is a religious leader, such as a minister, priest or other religious leader.
fact: «Chaplain» means a religious leader who works in a school, hospital, prison, army, university or sports team.
fact: Today, some chaplains serve people of all faiths and none, offering a listening ear.
fact: A school chaplain may lead prayers or assemblies, and a hospital chaplain may visit people who are ill.
fact: Phrases to know: school chaplain, hospital chaplain, army chaplain.
exercise: «A hospital chaplain is a religious leader who visits patients and families.» Where does this chaplain work? | At the bottom of the sea | At a bus stop | *In a hospital | In a bakery that sells bread
exercise: Which of these places could have a chaplain? | A bakery that sells only bread | A bicycle shop | A wooden bench in a park | *An army base
exercise: «Many hospitals have chaplains from different faiths.» What does faiths mean? | Patients | Hospitals | *Religions | Shops
test: What is a chaplain? | A teacher of maths | A doctor who only treats teeth | *A religious leader who works outside a church | A baker who makes bread
test: «Chaplains... comfort patients and families.» What does comfort mean here? | Ask them to leave | *Help them feel better when they are worried | Sell them food | Make them angry
exam: Why might a hospital chaplain visit a patient? | To teach them maths | To cut their hair | *To comfort them and listen | To sell medicine
